WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.080
So one of the great things
about being an entrepreneur

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.240
is that you don't have to pretend
to be someone you're not.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.560
You can build the culture around
things that you care about,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.800
build your own value system.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.880
You don't have to pretend
to be a suit in an office.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.200
The funny thing is that I don't
really feel very successful.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.480
I know I've been lucky
to build a company,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.480
and that company got sold
for a lot of money.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.240
But in my own head,
I still beat myself up and I think,

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.920
"Come on! You haven’t actually
contributed something to the world.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.960
You've got to do something
that's more meaningful,

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.720
make sure we don't screw
up the next 10, 20 years."

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.120
I think that's quite a good tension,

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.400
if you can make sure that
you channel it in a positive way

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.120
and not something that
whirs away in your head

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.480
and feels like a negative thought.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.280
Lastminute.com was really one of the
first e-commerce companies in Europe.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.800
We had to convince people,
back in 1998,

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:58.960
that people were going to
buy stuff

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.360
with their credit cards
on the internet.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.520
Can you imagine that?

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.560
Isn't there an awful lot of pressure
on you now?

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.840
Because this has become
a major company.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.040
There's always been a pressure on us,

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.960
but it's no worse than it's been
for the last couple of years.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.520
It's so hard when
you're in a start-up

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.760
because your personality

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.040
is part of how you market
and communicate.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.000
But if I look back, I think I put
myself out there a bit too much.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.000
When the stock market collapsed

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.520
and our share price went from
£5.35 to about 19p

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.520
I got a lot of attention
in the media,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.720
and I got a lot
of handwritten letters.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.120
I got 3,000 letters from
people writing to me

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.640
telling me I was an awful
person for taking their money.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.760
I was naive
in dealing with the media,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.200
and I was naive a bit in thinking
we could attract all this attention

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.200
and not meet the
consequences of that.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.280
So, be yourself,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.480
build things around
the values that you have,

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.840
but hold a little bit back.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.480
So in 2004, I just left my company,
Lastminute.com,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.760
and I was taking a few months off.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.040
And I was in Morocco
with my new boyfriend

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.400
and I fell out of a car.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.920
I wasn't wearing a seatbelt,
we skidded off the road.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.000
I broke 28 bones and I had a stroke.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.440
I had to then spend pretty much
the next two years in hospital,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.240
and the next
probably two years after that

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.160
in hospital in my own house

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.000
recovering from that
cataclysmically bad event.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.640
I was pretty out of it
for a long time in hospital

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.920
but I had decided I was going
to start another business

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.040
before I had the accident,
called Lucky Voice.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:34.920
It's a karaoke business,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.520
and the guy I was going
to start the business with

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.560
used to come to me in hospital

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.440
and start showing me kind of
designs and drawings,

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.800
and all the things
we were going to do.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.360
I was completely high on morphine

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.680
and I don't really remember
anything that I said to him.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.560
But it actually was
pretty important for me

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.280
because trying to rebuild your body,

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.920
but at the same time you want
to get your brain back a bit too.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.040
And I didn't want to be
slowly wasting away,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.120
just focusing on
whether I could stand up.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:59.440
I'd built an online
e-commerce business -

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.280
pretty much the most
techy thing you could do,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.920
and then all of a sudden it's
building bars in the real world.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.040
But I think being imaginative
in how you build your life

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.240
and your career is really rewarding
and actually quite important

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.560
in terms of how we build
resilience as human beings.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.800
I am the worst karaoke singer
you can possibly imagine.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.760
I pick things which
you can't really massacre,

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.840
and now post the accident I often
sing Elton John, I'm Still Standing,

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.440
for obvious reasons.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.280
Inspiration and things can come
from all kinds of surprising places.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.040
I've never really had a plan,
don't tell anyone.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.840
But I would really urge you
to be open-minded

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.400
about how you build your career
and about opportunities.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.360
So always take the call, always be
opportunistic, always be open-minded,

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.720
and talk to people and meet people

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.800
and don't feel like you have
to have a set way of doing things.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:50.920
The incredible thing about
being an entrepreneur

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.440
and understanding
a bit about technology

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.880
is that you see how quickly
things can change

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.480
and how innovation is possible.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.720
You don't have to be the person
doing the coding,

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.720
you can be the person working
in any aspect of technology.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.360
So don't shy away from technology

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.760
because it can help us
solve the big problems.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:07.880
That cat!

